The ordinary onboarded dir: logged in, never customised. claude writes .claude.json at
login and creates settings.json only when something is configured, so this shape is the
common case rather than an edge one.

An ABSENT settings.json is an answer here, not a gap — claude's defaults are no plugins,
no extra marketplaces, no denials and connectors on. The fixture exists because gating
those axes on the file existing turned this dir into four "unverified" lines against an
identical sibling, and masked a real connector split behind one of them.
